course: dictionary
lesson: 11495
title: Who is the aggressor?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An aggressor is a person, group or country that starts a fight, attack or war. To find the aggressor in a text, look for clues: who started it, who attacked first, and who was only defending themselves?
explain: «The aggressor threw the first punch, and the other boy only covered his face.» The clue is first punch. The boy who started the attack is the aggressor, even if he is not the biggest or the loudest.
explain: «The aggressor crossed the border with its army in the morning.» Here the clue is crossed the border. A country that moves its army in to attack is the aggressor, and the country it attacks is the one defending itself.
fact: An aggressor is the one who starts a fight, attack or war.
fact: Aggressor is a noun. You can have one aggressor or many aggressors.
fact: In history and the news, the aggressor is the side that attacked first.
fact: A person, a group or a country can each be an aggressor.
fact: Being bigger or louder does not make someone the aggressor. Starting the attack does.
exercise: «The aggressor threw the first punch.» What is an aggressor? | The referee who stops the fight | The one who gets hurt | The one who watches | *The one who starts the fight
exercise: News report: «Country B sent its army across the border into Country A.» Which country is the aggressor? | *Country B | Country A | Both countries | Neither country
exercise: «Sam pushed Tom first, and then Tom pushed back.» Who is the aggressor? | Both boys equally | Tom | Nobody | *Sam
test: A pack of wolves attacked the sheep first, and then the farmer's dog chased them away. Who is the aggressor? | The sheep | The farm | *The wolves | The farmer's dog
test: What does aggressor mean? | *A person, group or country that starts a fight, attack or war | A teacher who stops fights in the playground | A person who wins every game | A soldier who defends a city
exam: Which sentence best shows an aggressor? | The guard closed the gate to keep strangers out | *The boy who pushed a classmate first, so the classmate pushed back | A teacher stopped the two boys from arguing | The sheep ran into the field to escape the rain
